# Complete bank reconciliation — “not marked cleared”

## UI text

`Complete bank reconciliation`  
`21 bank transaction(s) not marked cleared.`

## Meaning

For the **selected Month-End period** (e.g. `2026-06`):

1. Count **bank statement lines only** (exclude Add Cash Expense).
2. Compare to Bank Reconciliation session `clearedTransactionIds`.
3. If no completed recon session (or lines not ticked cleared) → show uncleared count.

**Cleared** = user confirmed that line matches the bank statement / closing balance process in **Settings → Bank Reconciliation** (tick each line, then complete recon).

This is **not** the same as:

- Categorising for P&L / BAS (Biz Intel categories)
- Having uploaded/parsed the PDF (lines exist but may still be uncleared)

## Cash expense

Manual cash expenses are **never** required to be “cleared” — they are not on the bank PDF. Month with only cash → recon task can show done / “Cash Expense only”.

## SELPIC workflow

- Upload + classify → P&L/BAS numbers work even if uncleared > 0.
- Before **Lock accounting period**, clear bank lines for that month (or accept open period).
- 21 uncleared ≈ 21 bank rows in that month not yet ticked in recon UI.

## Code

- Checklist: `lib/subledger/month-end-checklist.ts` (`bank-recon` task)
- UI: `components/Reconciliation/BankReconciliationPanel.tsx`
- Storage: `clearedTransactionIds` on bank reconciliation session
